---
import MainLayout from "../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
import CSHero from "../components/CSHero.astro";
import CaseSideNav from "../components/CaseSideNav.astro";

const project = {
  number: "04",
  title: "Closing the ML Data Loop",
  headline: "I turned isolated model failures into a trackable data-improvement lifecycle.",
  breadcrumb: "AV MLOps / NVIDIA",
  role: "Product & service designer",
  duration: "Oct 2024–Mar 2025",
  cover: "/assets/mlloop/ml-data-loop-hero.png",
  excerpt:
    "Autonomous-driving teams could find model failures, but they could not follow the data used to address them across collection, annotation, training, and evaluation. I led the service and product design for a shared workspace that connected those steps around a persistent failure scenario.",
};

const sections = [
  { id: "context", label: "Why it mattered" },
  { id: "system", label: "Mapping the system" },
  { id: "prototype", label: "Proving the workflow" },
  { id: "collaboration", label: "Co-design" },
  { id: "solution", label: "Solution" },
  { id: "impact", label: "Impact" },
  { id: "reflection", label: "Reflection" },
];


const solutionViews = [
  {
    id: "context-view",
    label: "Customizable views",
    copy: "Data specialists could tailor the metadata shown for a review task, making large datasets easier to scan without forcing every workflow into the same display.",
    visual: "metadata",
  },
  {
    id: "analysis-view",
    label: "Model analysis",
    copy: "Reviewers could move from KPI trend analysis to the worst-performing examples, then inspect a single example in context.",
    visual: "analysis",
  },
  {
    id: "requests-view",
    label: "Data tracking",
    copy: "Teams could submit and track labeling or data-collection requests from the same workspace.",
    visual: "requests",
  },
];
---

<MainLayout title="Closing the ML Data Loop — Michelle Tenin">
  <div class="case-layout shell">
    <CaseSideNav {sections} />

    <div class="case-column">
      <CSHero {...project} />

      <article class="story">
        <section id="context">
          <div class="section-heading"><span>Why it mattered</span><i></i></div>
          <h2 class="display">A model failure is not always a model problem.</h2>
          <p>
            Issues found during road testing became engineering tickets. An engineer would adjust the model and test again—but some failures needed better or more representative data, not another round of parameter tuning.
          </p>
          <p>
            There was no scenario-level record connecting the issue to the data collected for it, the preparation work requested, or the model results that followed. Teams could track a ticket. They could not track the improvement cycle.
          </p>

          <div class="impact-preview" aria-label="Project impact">
            <div><strong>0 → ~30</strong><span>models with scenario tracking</span></div>
            <div><strong>Thousands</strong><span>of scenarios tracked</span></div>
            <div><strong>1 workspace</strong><span>connecting the data loop</span></div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="system">
          <div class="section-heading"><span>Mapping the system</span><i></i></div>
          <h2 class="display">I followed the data across teams—not just screens.</h2>
          <p>
            I interviewed model engineers, data specialists, engineering leadership, annotation operations, and data publishing teams. Journey mapping exposed where context disappeared as a scenario moved between people and systems.
          </p>
          <p>
            The design opportunity was to make the failure scenario a persistent unit of work: a shared thread connecting the data assembled for it, operational requests, released datasets, and evaluation evidence.
          </p>

          <figure class="system-map-figure">
            <div class="mockup-browser system-map-card">
              <div class="figma-document-bar">
                <span class="figma-mark" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
                <span class="figma-zoom">100%</span>
              </div>
              <div class="figma-canvas">
                <img src="/assets/mlloop/data-loop-ecosystem-mapping.png" alt="Blurred ecosystem map of data and model-development workflows" loading="lazy" />
              </div>
            </div>
            <figcaption>Ecosystem mapping exposed where data and context were lost across handoffs. Details intentionally obscured.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </section>

        <section id="prototype">
          <div class="section-heading"><span>Proving the workflow</span><i></i></div>
          <h2 class="display">Useful first. Integrated second.</h2>
          <p>
            Many capabilities began as lightweight spreadsheet or notebook workflows. These prototypes let the team test whether a workflow was useful before investing in the APIs and large-scale data operations needed to support it in the shared interface.
          </p>

          <div class="prototype-path" aria-label="Path from workflow prototype to integrated product">
            <div><strong>Spreadsheet and notebook workflows</strong><span>Test the task with real data</span></div>
            <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
            <div><strong>Working interface prototypes</strong><span>Refine the interaction in code</span></div>
            <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
            <div><strong>Production workspace</strong><span>Build the supporting services</span></div>
          </div>

          <p>
            This approach also clarified product boundaries. The workspace needed to support operational curation, while deeper exploratory analysis was often better served by dedicated analytics tools.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="collaboration">
          <div class="section-heading"><span>Co-design</span><i></i></div>
          <h2 class="display">Tight collaboration made the service real.</h2>
          <p>
            The product was shaped alongside the data specialists who would operate it. We reviewed ideas as they emerged—from dataset curation to comparing reference labels with model output—and iterated before the workflows hardened into infrastructure.
          </p>
          <p>
            During an onsite hackathon, the team brought one collaboration feature from idea to a working flow in a week. A data specialist could share curated samples with a model engineer, receive flagged examples asynchronously, refine the data-mining query, and then send the improved dataset for managed annotation.
          </p>

          <figure class="feedback-figure">
            <div class="feedback-card">
              <img src="/assets/mlloop/hackathon-data-operations-flow.png" alt="Data specialist and model engineer dataset review loop leading to managed annotation" loading="lazy" />
            </div>
            <figcaption>Example data operations flow targeted during hackathon</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </section>

        <section id="solution">
          <div class="section-heading"><span>Solution</span><i></i></div>
          <h2 class="display">One workspace for the full improvement loop.</h2>
          <p>
            The final experience brought curation, operational requests, and evaluation into one scenario-centered workflow. The highlights below show three of the most useful interface capabilities without trying to replace every specialized system around them.
          </p>

          <div class="solution-switcher">
            <div class="solution-tabs tabs tabs-lift" aria-label="Solution capabilities">
              {solutionViews.map((view, index) => (
                <>
                  <input
                    type="radio"
                    name="solution-tabs"
                    class="tab"
                    aria-label={view.label}
                    checked={index === 0}
                  />
                  <article class="tab-content solution-panel">
                    <p class="solution-intro">{view.copy}</p>

                    {view.visual === "metadata" && (
                      <figure class="solution-figure">
                        <div class="feature-visual solution-ui-visual metadata-focus">
                          <img src="/assets/mlloop/solution-metadata-views.png" alt="Fictionalized dataset workspace focused on metadata display controls" loading="lazy" />
                        </div>
                      </figure>
                    )}

                    {view.visual === "analysis" && (
                      <figure class="solution-figure">
                        <div class="feature-visual solution-ui-visual analysis-focus">
                          <img src="/assets/mlloop/solution-model-analysis.png" alt="Fictionalized KPI analysis view focused on opening worst-performing samples" loading="lazy" />
                        </div>
                      </figure>
                    )}

                    {view.visual === "requests" && (
                      <figure class="solution-figure">
                        <div class="feature-visual solution-ui-visual requests-focus">
                          <img src="/assets/mlloop/solution-data-requests.png" alt="Fictionalized dataset status view focused on curation progress and labeling requests" loading="lazy" />
                        </div>
                      </figure>
                    )}
                    <p class="solution-disclaimer">Simplified recreation shown to protect proprietary information.</p>
                  </article>
                </>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="impact">
          <div class="section-heading"><span>Impact</span><i></i></div>
          <h2 class="display">Scenario tracking became a shared foundation.</h2>
          <p>
            By the end of the project, the organization had moved from no scenario-centered tracking to a central workspace spanning approximately 30 models and thousands of scenarios.
          </p>

          <div class="outcomes">
            <div><h3>Connected systems</h3><p>Collection, annotation, dataset publishing, and evaluation gained shared connection points.</p></div>
            <div><h3>Self-service visibility</h3><p>Model engineers could observe data work and follow progress without relying on disconnected status updates.</p></div>
            <div><h3>Persistent tracking</h3><p>Teams could follow a failure scenario across repeated data and model iterations.</p></div>
          </div>

          <blockquote>The workspace became the de facto scenario-centered data-management tool.</blockquote>
        </section>

        <section id="reflection">
          <div class="section-heading"><span>Reflection</span><i></i></div>
          <h2 class="display">The interface was only the visible layer.</h2>
          <p>
            My work ranged from journey mapping and information architecture to coded prototypes, interview plans, engineering handoff, and UI quality assurance. The harder design problem was aligning services, teams, and feedback loops around the same unit of work.
          </p>
          <p>
            We deliberately deferred synthetic-data supplementation until the core lifecycle had been proven with collected data. Establishing reliable tracking first created a foundation for a more automated improvement loop later.
          </p>
          <p>
            The system’s value is also reflected in what came next. I am now working on a second phase that explores how these learnings can support physical AI model development across the company, along with other foundation-model workflows. The goal is to carry the core principles forward in an approach that is less specific to autonomous driving.
          </p>
        </section>

        <nav class="next" aria-label="Previous and next case studies">
          <a href="/unified-data-workspace">← Data Platform Hub</a>
          <a href="/aurora">Cancer Survivorship Support →</a>
        </nav>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</MainLayout>

<script>
  const nav = document.querySelector<HTMLOListElement>("[data-case-nav]");
  if (nav) {
    const ids: string[] = JSON.parse(nav.dataset.sections ?? "[]");
    const links = Array.from(nav.querySelectorAll<HTMLAnchorElement>("a"));
    const indicator = nav.parentElement?.querySelector<HTMLElement>(".side-track span");

    const activate = (id: string) => {
      links.forEach((link) => link.toggleAttribute("aria-current", link.hash === `#${id}`));
      const active = links.find((link) => link.hash === `#${id}`);
      const item = active?.closest("li");
      if (!item || !indicator) return;
      const listRect = nav.getBoundingClientRect();
      const itemRect = item.getBoundingClientRect();
      indicator.style.transform = `translateY(${itemRect.top - listRect.top + (itemRect.height - indicator.offsetHeight) / 2}px)`;
    };

    const observer = new IntersectionObserver(
      (entries) => {
        const visible = entries.find((entry) => entry.isIntersecting);
        if (visible) activate(visible.target.id);
      },
      { rootMargin: "-15% 0px -65% 0px" }
    );

    ids.forEach((id) => {
      const section = document.getElementById(id);
      if (section) observer.observe(section);
    });
    activate(ids[0]);
  }

</script>

<style>
  .case-layout{--accent:#2c6bed;--visual-bg:#f3f6fb;--visual-border:color-mix(in srgb,var(--ink) 10%,transparent);position:relative;display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px minmax(0,48rem) 180px;justify-content:center;gap:2.5rem}
  .case-column{grid-column:2;min-width:0}
  .case-column :global(.case-cover){aspect-ratio:4/3;max-height:none;object-fit:cover;object-position:left top;border-radius:var(--radius-box)}
  .story section{scroll-margin-top:2rem;padding:5rem 0 0}
  .section-heading{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.8rem;margin-bottom:1rem;font-size:.82rem;font-weight:650;color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--ink) 72%,transparent)}
  .section-heading i{display:block;flex:1;height:1px;background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--ink) 8%,transparent)}
  .story h2{max-width:42rem;margin:.25rem 0 1rem;font-size:1.65rem;line-height:1.35;letter-spacing:-.02em}
  .story section>p{max-width:44rem;margin:.65rem 0;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.55rem}
  blockquote{margin:2rem 0 0;padding:.25rem 0 .25rem 1.25rem;border-left:2px solid var(--ink);font:400 1.1rem/1.55 var(--font-display)}
  .impact-preview{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1.5rem;margin:2.25rem 0 .25rem;padding:1.5rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--visual-border);border-bottom:1px solid var(--visual-border)}
  .impact-preview strong{display:block;font:400 1.6rem/1 var(--font-display)}.impact-preview span{display:block;margin-top:.45rem;font-size:.68rem;line-height:1rem;color:var(--muted)}
  .system-map-figure{margin:2rem 0}
  .system-map-card{overflow:hidden;border:1px solid #3f3f3f;border-radius:var(--radius-box);background:#202020;box-shadow:none}
  .system-map-card.mockup-browser{padding:0!important}
  .figma-document-bar{position:relative;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;min-height:38px;margin:0;padding:0 .85rem;background:#2c2c2c;color:#f1f1f1;border-bottom:1px solid #444}
  .figma-zoom{justify-self:end;font-size:.56rem;color:#b8b8b8}
  .figma-mark{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,5px);grid-template-rows:repeat(3,5px);width:10px;height:15px}.figma-mark i{display:block}.figma-mark i:nth-child(1){grid-column:1;grid-row:1;background:#f24e1e;border-radius:3px 0 0 3px}.figma-mark i:nth-child(2){grid-column:2;grid-row:1;background:#ff7262;border-radius:0 3px 3px 0}.figma-mark i:nth-child(3){grid-column:1;grid-row:2;background:#a259ff;border-radius:3px 0 0 3px}.figma-mark i:nth-child(4){grid-column:2;grid-row:2;background:#1abcfe;border-radius:50%}.figma-mark i:nth-child(5){grid-column:1;grid-row:3;background:#0acf83;border-radius:3px 0 3px 3px}
  .figma-canvas{margin:0;padding:0;background:#f7f7f8}
  .figma-canvas img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:contain;border:0;background:#fff}
  .system-map-figure figcaption{margin-top:.5rem;font-size:.75rem;line-height:1.15rem;color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--ink) 45%,transparent)}
  .prototype-path{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr;align-items:center;gap:1rem;margin:2rem 0}
  .prototype-path>div{min-height:105px;padding:1.1rem;background:var(--color-base-200);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-box)}.prototype-path strong{display:block;font-size:.73rem;line-height:1.05rem}.prototype-path span{display:block;margin-top:.5rem;font-size:.64rem;line-height:1rem;color:var(--muted)}.prototype-path>i{font-style:normal;color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--ink) 30%,transparent)}
  .feedback-figure{margin:2rem 0}
  .feedback-card{padding:1.25rem;overflow:hidden;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-box);background:var(--color-base-200)}
  .feedback-card img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:contain}
  .feedback-figure figcaption{margin-top:.5rem;font-size:.75rem;line-height:1.15rem;color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--ink) 45%,transparent)}
  .solution-switcher{margin-top:2rem}.solution-tabs{--tab-p:.85rem;--border:1px;width:100%;align-items:flex-start}
  .solution-tabs.tabs-lift>input.tab{flex:0 0 auto;justify-content:flex-start;width:auto;min-height:46px;height:46px;font:600 .68rem/1rem var(--font-sans);text-align:left;white-space:nowrap}.solution-tabs.tabs-lift>input.tab:checked{border-radius:8px 8px 0 0}.solution-tabs.tabs-lift>input.tab:checked::before{display:none!important;content:none!important}
  .solution-panel{overflow:hidden;padding:1.25rem;border-color:var(--color-base-300);background:var(--color-base-100)}.solution-intro{max-width:44rem;margin:.65rem 0 1.25rem;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.55rem}
  .solution-figure{margin:0}.solution-disclaimer{margin:.65rem 0 0;font-size:.75rem;line-height:1.15rem;color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--ink) 45%,transparent)}
  .feature-visual{height:400px;overflow:hidden;border:1px solid var(--visual-border);border-radius:var(--radius-box);background:var(--visual-bg)}
  .solution-ui-visual{position:relative;background:var(--color-base-100)}.solution-ui-visual img{position:absolute;display:block;max-width:none;height:auto}.solution-ui-visual::after{position:absolute;z-index:1;inset:-1px;content:"";pointer-events:none;background:linear-gradient(to right,var(--color-base-100) 0,transparent 18%,transparent 82%,var(--color-base-100) 100%),linear-gradient(to bottom,var(--color-base-100) 0,transparent 20%,transparent 80%,var(--color-base-100) 100%)}
  .metadata-focus img{top:50%;left:0;width:190%;transform:translateY(-39%)}
  .analysis-focus img{right:0;bottom:0;width:110%}
  .requests-focus img{top:50%;left:50%;width:140%;transform:translate(-43%,-37%)}
  .outcomes{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1.75rem;margin-top:2rem}.outcomes h3{margin:0 0 .5rem;font-size:.76rem}.outcomes p{margin:0;font-size:.69rem;line-height:1.2rem;color:var(--muted)}
  .next{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:1rem;border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin-top:4rem;padding:1.5rem 0 2rem}.next a{font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);text-decoration:none}
  @media(max-width:1100px){.case-layout{display:block;width:min(48rem,calc(100% - 48px))}}
  @media(max-width:700px){
    .case-layout{width:min(100% - 28px,48rem)}.story section{padding-top:3.75rem}.impact-preview,.outcomes{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:1.25rem}.impact-preview div+div{padding-top:1.1rem;border-top:1px solid var(--visual-border)}
    .prototype-path{grid-template-columns:1fr}.prototype-path>i{transform:rotate(90deg);text-align:center}.figma-document-bar{min-height:34px}.feedback-card{padding:.85rem}
    .solution-tabs{--tab-p:.55rem}.solution-tabs.tabs-lift>input.tab{min-height:50px;height:50px;font-size:.61rem}.solution-panel{padding:.85rem}.feature-visual{height:330px}
  }
</style>
